<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Classification remains mixed by endpoint. Stage/branch macro-F1 is highest for diffusion-style baselines (Palantir and Scanpy-DPT), while raw-expression is highest on stage balanced accuracy. The extracted cell head remains strongest on branch balanced accuracy, CD4/CD8 AUROC, and mono/macro AUROC.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For pseudotime-depth ordering, the extracted cell head leads all compared methods. Because pseudotime orientation is arbitrary across donor-local evaluations (each donor’s pseudotime is computed independently, and the algorithm may assign increasing values toward either stem or mature cells), we report the orientation-independent <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\rho|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\rho|</annotation></semantics></math> (see Section <a href="#Sx1.SSx17" title="S17. Metric-level paired significance, orientation summary, and classification deltas ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Discovery of a Hematopoietic Manifold in scGPT Yields a Method for Extracting Performant Algorithms from Biological Foundation Model Internals" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">S17. Metric-level paired significance, orientation summary, and classification deltas</span></a> for the full orientation analysis): the cell head achieves <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\rho|{=}0.439" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.439</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\rho|{=}0.439</annotation></semantics></math> versus <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.364" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.364</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.364</annotation></semantics></math> (hybrid), <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.331" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.331</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.331</annotation></semantics></math> (Palantir), <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.279" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.279</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.279</annotation></semantics></math> (SVD), <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.274" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.274</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.274</annotation></semantics></math> (scVI), <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.266" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.266</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.266</annotation></semantics></math> (raw), <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.261" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.261</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.261</annotation></semantics></math> (DPT), <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.259" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.259</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.259</annotation></semantics></math> (PCA), <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.253" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.253</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.253</annotation></semantics></math> (CellTypist), and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.235" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.235</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.235</annotation></semantics></math> (anchor). In paired split-level tests versus the cell head, all method-minus-head deltas are negative with Wilcoxon BH-<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\leq 2.7\times 10^{-7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2.7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\leq 2.7\times 10^{-7}</annotation></semantics></math> in the 88-split pooled analysis (Table <a href="#S3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 3.3 The extracted algorithm is competitive ‣ 3 Results ‣ Discovery of a Hematopoietic Manifold in scGPT Yields a Method for Extracting Performant Algorithms from Biological Foundation Model Internals" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and Figure <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3.3 The extracted algorithm is competitive ‣ 3 Results ‣ Discovery of a Hematopoietic Manifold in scGPT Yields a Method for Extracting Performant Algorithms from Biological Foundation Model Internals" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
