<div id="Sx1.SSx17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx17.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The orientation-aware view preserves the same ranking at the top: the cell head has both the highest signed mean and the highest absolute mean (<math id="Sx1.SSx17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\rho|=0.439" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.439</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\rho|=0.439</annotation></semantics></math>). Several baselines show non-trivial absolute association (for example Palantir <math id="Sx1.SSx17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\rho|=0.331" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.331</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\rho|=0.331</annotation></semantics></math>) but with weaker sign stability (positive-share near 35–52%), consistent with frequent orientation reversals across donor-local evaluations.</p>
</div>
