<div id="Sx1.SSx20.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx20.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The 10D+MLP2 variant exceeds the frozen-scGPT baseline on 7/8 pooled metrics with 6/8 BH-significant after paired splitwise correction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SSx21" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">S21. Probe-depth comparison</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SSx21.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx21.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We closed the downstream probe-depth question on the broader 40-split Robust-V2 family. We evaluated the robust linear extracted head against both a modest non-linear readout (MLP2, <math id="Sx1.SSx21.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\rightarrow 64\rightarrow C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\rightarrow 64\rightarrow C</annotation></semantics></math>) and a deeper alternative (MLP3, <math id="Sx1.SSx21.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\rightarrow 128\rightarrow 64\rightarrow C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>128</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\rightarrow 128\rightarrow 64\rightarrow C</annotation></semantics></math>). Neither nonlinear probe becomes the new default: MLP2 yields BH-significant gains on CD4/CD8 AUROC (<math id="Sx1.SSx21.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.0045" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.0045</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.0045</annotation></semantics></math>) and CD4/CD8 balanced accuracy (<math id="Sx1.SSx21.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.0049" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.0049</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.0049</annotation></semantics></math>), but significantly worsens mono/macro balanced accuracy (<math id="Sx1.SSx21.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.0076" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.0076</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.0076</annotation></semantics></math>) and both stage endpoints. We therefore keep the linear 10D head as the main robust classifier result, and treat MLP2 as the best targeted nonlinear follow-up when CD4/CD8 discrimination is the priority.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10261v1/fig_head10d_probe_depth_tradeoff.png" id="Sx1.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/345;" width="476" height="345" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Probe-depth tradeoff for the extracted 10D H65 cell head on the 40-split Robust-V2 family. The linear head remains the best overall default.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SSx22" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">S22. Direct learnability baseline</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SSx22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx22.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To test whether a comparably small model trained directly on raw expression would recover the same task structure, we trained two direct raw-expression baselines on the same 12 grouped donor-holdout splits: a 1-hidden-layer model (<math id="Sx1.SSx22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1200\rightarrow 64\rightarrow C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1200</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1200\rightarrow 64\rightarrow C</annotation></semantics></math>) and a 2-hidden-layer model (<math id="Sx1.SSx22.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1200\rightarrow 128\rightarrow 64\rightarrow C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1200</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>128</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1200\rightarrow 128\rightarrow 64\rightarrow C</annotation></semantics></math>), both on <math id="Sx1.SSx22.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1+x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+x)</annotation></semantics></math> input.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx1.T18" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 18: </span>Repeated grouped-split comparison between direct tiny-from-scratch raw-expression MLPs, frozen scGPT avg-pool + MLP, and the extracted 10D head + MLP2. Values are pooled donor-level means across 12 splits.</figcaption>
